  "id": "Compound::DB01274 - Disease::DOID:3083",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Arformoterol and Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) through its inclusion in the class of adrenergic beta-2 agonists, which are known to treat COPD. Arformoterol, as an adrenergic beta-2 agonist, is associated with the treatment of COPD, as indicated by the direct treatment relationship between Formoterol and COPD in multiple paths. Additionally, the presence of Arformoterol in the adrenergic beta-2 agonist class, along with its role in causing Digitalis Intoxication, further supports its classification and potential therapeutic use. The overlapping pathways highlight the shared mechanisms of action and therapeutic applications among these compounds, reinforcing the likelihood of a relationship between Arformoterol and COPD. However, the evidence is limited to the specific relationships observed in the dataset, and further research is needed to confirm the therapeutic relevance of Arformoterol in COPD treatment.",
